d":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HitomiTenshi","html_url":"https://github.com/HitomiTenshi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HitomiTenshi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HitomiTenshi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HitomiTenshi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HitomiTenshi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HitomiTenshi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HitomiTenshi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HitomiTenshi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HitomiTenshi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HitomiTenshi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-04-18T09:12:04Z","updated_at":"2019-04-18T09:12:04Z","body":"@JoostK I dug a little deeper and it seems that if you have `\"target\": \"es2015\"` in your `tsconfig.app.json`, the command `ng build --prod` will overwrite `.d.ts` files in `./node_modules` in a weird way, essentially removing `BrowserAnimationsModule` from `./node_modules/@angular/platform-browser/animations/animations.d.ts`.\r\n\r\nRecovering from that is impossible. You will need to delete the `node_modules` folder and run `npm install` again to fix it.\r\n\r\nIf you set `\"target\": \"es5\"` in your `tsconfig.app.json`, then this bug does not happen.\r\n\r\nMy Setup:\r\n- Windows 10\r\n- Node 11.14.0\r\n- Using the same angular versions as OP","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/484420080/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"HitomiTenshi","id":7304212,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMDQyMTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7304212?v